  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "02b9c659-5dad-4fe4-b319-ed83689b3ec2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the region heads, each measured by both; so is every Euclidean head, \
through the support of its vertex density"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"50bfdfff-8d73-4352-907f-d012bfcef266"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b0264c9-259a-4241-9f76-4500a7fc5467"],
 ", Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d844127d-dd30-4503-b5dd-5e09ae828f55"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c2ea01cc-e8b2-4b94-8046-e396b853a8db"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular lattice, before the rim, and is \
the convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction; on the \
hexagonal lattice it is measured, not proved."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a789e6d1-4b41-477e-80ef-c0808fa67e3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Shell on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32d07157-237b-44e4-a899-82803d779e34"],
 ", the coordination sequence; Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f6cdf00-45c6-4040-bb32-c6efcd52b909"],
 ", since a shell is all boundary."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"49a122ae-374e-44e9-9c9e-17da41872286"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Segment on the square grid between vertices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49a5ef4e-eb2b-4e8b-a208-331046e57b6f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38e7c995-2a63-44b7-a1c9-08740e4ff5ea"],
 " steps apart along the two axes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "1"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b279659-c6cf-4fb7-9080-c09cbbdf96ef"],
 ": its interval is a rectangle, with counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d33c2530-4593-44e5-9137-3162d06da44d"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0e97da2-2357-47b8-a3de-179e1da91895"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"7ad68907-e787-44ce-a096-4b7308b90ed6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the discretized plane: the Riemannian measure can exceed the \
counting measure of the smaller ball, when a vertex at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23a7e329-4c8e-40aa-b97b-618911456ec8"],
 " has no neighbour at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a5aa88cf-7d13-4a89-a7e5-bc7b7594e563"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"330953bb-fd2a-4f67-a3cd-3009faf7b545"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["VolumeGrowthObservables"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/VolumeGrowthObservables", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "50a628c5-65fb-4efd-b007-ab50d34f25a7"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the dimension and the scalar curvature read from the growth of the balls \
under either measure; it lives on the Riemannian Infrageometry guide"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"4a4da6a5-1d24-4294-ab82-86bdd4139543"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Find Functions", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"a091e59e-28e9-4675-aae4-6330d0044e6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraPoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraPoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "754b0220-16c6-4d2f-986d-ea5a1ad13694"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a vertex drawn from the candidate pool, narrowed by \"From\" and \"Distance\
\"; a trailing count gives a List of vertices"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"4ebf733a-5742-4c6a-8ebd-16c7eac15e18"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraMidpoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraMidpoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "5f9782ac-c588-4ac5-a34a-18f209b996b8"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the middle vertices of the shortest paths from p1 to p2 as a density, one \
vertex at even distance, two at odd"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"0bc95792-c7fe-4157-8cd5-fe2360de3803"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraEquidistantSet"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraEquidistantSet", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "a17e4a42-50ef-4f52-bf7f-e53d76038414"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the vertices equidistant from p1, \[Ellipsis], pn, as a sorted vertex list; \
a trailing {lo, hi} thickens each bisector to a slab"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"0f045ade-e741-49ec-9fff-39d29b5195d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraSphere"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraSphere", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "6c099e0b-8c33-42b6-a822-208edd8412c2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "n inclusion-minimal connected subsets of the shell of c that separate its \
inside from its outside; Properties chooses the class, \"NextVertexFunction\" \
the order of the peel"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"dc3211c1-ad98-4c63-8f58-49c96fd5adee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraSegment"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraSegment", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "e90675a3-c3bd-4bf0-8ff5-1fc776968931"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one shortest path from p to q as a vertex list; a trailing count gives a \
List of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"e56141a5-8354-4caa-90a9-17b64e911c19"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRay"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRay", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "7e408da0-5993-4b94-a654-50808ad86aee"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one ray from p through q as a vertex list, a shortest path from p through q \
that no neighbour of its last vertex prolongs; a trailing count gives a List \
of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"1282eba6-06f3-4cc2-97b1-2d5794a822df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraLine"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraLine", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "9a6ce069-61c6-43e9-80e7-d1048b8d5454"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one line through p and q as a vertex list, an inextensible shortest path \
through both; a trailing count gives a List of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"cd79649b-dcba-4e10-9e92-a2f718b4e5ec"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Measurements", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"e789557c-154c-4556-a44c-0e418552d104"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "3ea1ac99-4438-4fc3-b53a-9c3f4b5f4bc9"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a property of a head on a graph: \"Graph\", \"Cardinality\", \"Length\", \
\"VertexDensity\", \"EdgeDensity\", \"Subgraph\", \"Faithful\", \
\"CountingMeasure\" and \"RiemannianMeasure\"; a List of properties gives an \
Association, All gives every property"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"23931f99-b2c0-4c65-85a9-873c588fed0c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraDensity"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDensity", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "9133e18b-69e1-4601-a3f6-0ce676b5ed73"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the marginal of any shape to the vertex set with respect to the counting \
measure: a vertex, a vertex list, a density, a walk graph; the one coercion \
in the API"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"b40fdb27-a10c-44b0-80e9-ef2aa0961763"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRepresentative"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRepresentative", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
